4.Write CSS selectors to style all elements with the class 'playlist-item' (for a Spotify playlist page) to have a dark background and white text. 
Then, add a rule to highlight the currently playing song with a different color using a unique id selector.
Ans.
<html>
<head>
  <style>
    .playlist-item {
      background-color: #181818; 
      color: #ffffff;          
      padding: 12px 18px;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
      border-radius: 6px;
    }

    #currently-playing {
      background-color: #1db954; 
      color: #000000;          
      font-weight: bold;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="playlist-item">1. Blinding Lights - The Weeknd</div>
  <div class="playlist-item" id="currently-playing">2. Starboy - The Weeknd</div>
  <div class="playlist-item">3. As It Was - Harry Styles</div>
</body>
</html>


5.Implement a simple light/dark mode switch for a BookMyShow movie detail page using internal CSS and a toggle button. When the button is clicked, 
switch between light and dark color themes for the page.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Use JavaScript to add or remove a 'dark-mode' class on the <body> 
and define the color themes in CSS.</em>
Ans.
<html>
<head>
  <title>BookMyShow Theme Switcher</title>
  <style>
    body {
      background-color: #ffffff;
      color: #222222;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      transition: background-color 0.3s, color 0.3s;
    }

    body.dark-mode {
      background-color: #121212;
      color: #ffffff;
    }

    .theme-btn {
      padding: 10px 20px;
      cursor: pointer;
      border-radius: 20px;
      border: none;
      background-color: #f84464;
      color: white;
      font-weight: bold;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>BookMyShow: Movie Details</h1>
  <button class="theme-btn" onclick="toggleTheme()">Toggle Dark/Light Mode</button>

  <script>
    function toggleTheme() {
      document.body.classList.toggle('dark-mode');
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
